  "id": 203711644573503,
  "uuid": "c76dc244-2352-4ba9-af3f-51a478bf5651",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "22a86897-ccb0-242e-2382-d6a3f7299e92",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "c9d60151-e294-eb13-a345-cb4857edd3a8",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The Community Health Management Association (CHMA) collaborated with AKU in the organisation of the event which involved community members, children from local schools, the Union Council Nazim and the Counsellors, CHS Residents and Masters Students and CHS faculty and staff.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Dr Gregory Pappas, Director of CHS, who was present at the occasion to support the community members in this initiative, remarked: \"It is important to involve the community in garbage disposal activity, and to disseminate education that would help resolve the problem of environmental hygiene by promoting a sustainable community participation process. I hope this event will galvanise the community to hold monthly Cleanliness Days.\"",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Mr Mairajuddin, Nazim, and Mr Shah Nawaz Jadoon, Naib Nazim, UC 2, along with the counsellors appreciated the efforts by AKU and the community on Cleanliness Day in Sultanabad. They encouraged the community to continue this practice and promised that all the facilities and logistics would be provided in the upcoming programmes of cleanliness in the area.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Mr Sultan, President of CHMA Sultanabad, said, \"CHMS has been working with AKU for the last 10 years for the betterment of the health and socio-economic status of Sultanabad. We will continue to focus on cleanliness and provide every support to AKU, the community and the Nazim to improve the garbage disposal system of the area.\"",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Dr. Khalil Qureshi from CHS presented a demonstration on how to pick up garbage and school children made speeches on the importance of cleanliness. The members then divided into four groups and each group chose an alley to clean. Tetley Tea sponsored the programme.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The programme is expected to increase awareness among the local people about the hazards of improper waste disposal to public health and enhance their knowledge on environmental health issues.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
